# Vibe engineering Effect apps

Michael argues that an agent should learn a fast-moving library from its source repository rather than trust stale model knowledge or a giant prompt. [08:51](https://youtu.be/Wmp2Tku2PrI?t=531) [12:59](https://youtu.be/Wmp2Tku2PrI?t=779)

He describes repository feedback from diagnostics, tests, lint rules, saved patterns, and short-lived contexts. Later, he recommends choosing patterns for the project and model rather than copying a universal pack. [30:30](https://youtu.be/Wmp2Tku2PrI?t=1830) [38:15](https://youtu.be/Wmp2Tku2PrI?t=2295) [58:08](https://youtu.be/Wmp2Tku2PrI?t=3488)
